// bubbler profile: lutris
//
// Lutris itself is a GTK app, but every Wine or Proton game it starts is
// an X11 client — Wine's X11 driver takes precedence over its Wayland one
// whenever DISPLAY is set (Arch wiki, Wine#Wayland) — so this profile
// grants `x11 "host"`, with the isolation caveat that carries: X11
// clients can keylog and inject into each other. The nested server
// bubbler starts by default has no window manager, which is what a game
// that maps and resizes its own windows expects.
//
// Sound is `pulseaudio`. The grant binds $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/pulse/native —
// the socket PipeWire's pulse server holds on a PipeWire host — and sets
// PULSE_SERVER to it, which is the path a libpulse client takes, as Wine
// and the Proton runtimes are. That socket carries capture as well as
// playback, so it is the microphone too. Not measured here: if a game is
// silent, add `pipewire` beside it.
//
// umu, Proton and DXVK's 32-bit path make i386 syscalls; the default
// filter carries i386 as well as x86_64, so they are filtered rather than
// killed. Never add `userns "disable"` — those runtimes nest
// pressure-vessel's own bubblewrap.
//
// ~/Games is Lutris's own convention for the install directory, and a
// missing share source is an error rather than a skipped bind, so create
// it (`mkdir ~/Games`) or edit the node to the directory you use. A prefix
// or library outside the home is named explicitly, e.g.
//   path-share "/kioxia/Games" mode=rw
//
// Bare by design. Add:
//   dbus {
//       own "net.lutris.Lutris"
//       talk "com.feralinteractive.GameMode"
//       talk "org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver"
//   }
//     — Lutris's own name (a second `lutris` and the lutris:// handler
//       reach the running one through it), the GameMode daemon, which
//       simply resolves to nothing where gamemoded is not installed, and
//       the screensaver blocker a running game holds.
//   portals
//     — Lutris calls the portals itself, for the file chooser among other
//       things. Not measured: a Proton or umu game brings
//       pressure-vessel, the same steam-runtime-tools that refuses to run
//       where /.flatpak-info exists (see `steam`), so this grant is also
//       what to drop first if a game stops with a Flatpak complaint.
//       Needs `dbus`.
//   system-bus {
//       see "org.freedesktop.UDisks2"
//       call "org.freedesktop.UDisks2=org.freedesktop.DBus.ObjectManager.GetManagedObjects@/org/freedesktop/UDisks2"
//   }
//     — the drive list Wine builds from UDisks2: `see` plus that one
//       ObjectManager call, and no more. A `talk` there would reach loop
//       setup, mount and LUKS unlock, which polkit judges as you.
//   notify
//     — install and download notifications. Needs `dbus`.
//   tray
//     — the tray icon. Needs `dbus`.
//   pipewire
//     — a game speaking PipeWire itself, and the screen-share portal.
lint-allow "x11-without-reason" reason="Wine and Proton games are X11 clients that want a window manager; a nested x11 with wm= is the alternative"
wayland
x11 "host"
dri
pulseaudio
network
gamepad
home-share "Games" mode=rw
desktop "net.lutris.Lutris.desktop"
command "lutris"
